From: Anthony Giacalone <anthony.giacalone@csulb.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] ES: a launch from the HTTP API starts at once, not at the next full minute

A launch through ES's HTTP API (POST /launch) started at the next full minute while the menu was idle. Two causes:

- Window::postToUiThread woke the main loop with PowerSaver's refresh event, which does nothing while the power
  saver is paused or off. It now also pushes an event of its own, so the wait returns within one 16 ms poll.
- The launch then did ~6 s of work on the UI thread before its transition started, longer than the power saver's
  awake time after an event (3 s in "enhanced"), so the loop went into standby with the transition unfinished and
  the game waited for the next minute's wake (es-rgds-powersaver's clock wake). A pending launch
  (ViewController::launchPending, capped at 10 s like es-rgds-launchonce) now counts as activity.

A button press always woke the menu; this is for launches from the network (the Store, scripts, tools/smoke.sh).

---
diff --git a/es-app/src/main.cpp b/es-app/src/main.cpp
index 2f65ba6e..71f77f2b 100644
--- a/es-app/src/main.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/main.cpp
@@ -760,6 +760,13 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[])
 	{
 		SDL_Event event;
 
+		// ROCKNIXDS (es-rgds-apiwake): a launch's transition must run to its end. A launch from the HTTP API runs on the
+		// UI thread after the request's wake event, and its own work (~6 s on an RG DS Plus before the transition starts)
+		// outlasted the power saver's awake time after that event (3 s, "enhanced"): the loop went into standby with the
+		// transition unfinished and the game only started at the next minute's wake. Count a pending launch as activity.
+		if (ViewController::launchPending())
+			ps_time = SDL_GetTicks();
+
 		int screenSaverTimeout = screensaver.getNextUpdateTimeout();
 		bool screenSaverWait = screenSaverTimeout > 0;
 
diff --git a/es-app/src/views/ViewController.h b/es-app/src/views/ViewController.h
index 3e802ed2..838520d4 100644
--- a/es-app/src/views/ViewController.h
+++ b/es-app/src/views/ViewController.h
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@ public:
 	// a steady clock in ms: not SDL_GetTicks, which starts again when ES re-initialises SDL around a game it closes its
 	// window for (every launch but DraStic's fast switch)
 	static long long monoMs();
+	// ROCKNIXDS (es-rgds-apiwake): a launch's transition is running (started under 10 s ago; past that it was cancelled
+	// and the flag left set). The main loop stays out of power-saver standby meanwhile, or the transition stalls.
+	static bool launchPending() { return GuiComponent::isLaunchTransitionRunning && sLaunchStartedAt != 0 && monoMs() - sLaunchStartedAt < 10000; }
 	
 	static void saveState();
 
diff --git a/es-core/src/Window.cpp b/es-core/src/Window.cpp
index 2ce73c91..3206964f 100644
--- a/es-core/src/Window.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/Window.cpp
@@ -1246,6 +1246,20 @@ void Window::postToUiThread(const std::function<void()>& func, void* data)
 	}
 	else // ROCKNIXDS: in power-saver standby the main loop only wakes on an event; a launch from the HTTP API waited up
 		PowerSaver::pushRefreshEvent();   // to a minute for it otherwise (no-op if one is already pending)
+
+	// ROCKNIXDS (es-rgds-apiwake.patch): wake the main loop whatever the power saver's state. pushRefreshEvent does
+	// nothing while the power saver is paused or off, and the slideshow screensaver's wait sleeps until its clock next
+	// changes (es-rgds-slideshow-wake.patch): a launch from the HTTP API then started at the next full minute. An event
+	// of our own makes the wait return within a poll (16 ms); the loop ignores its type and runs this function.
+	static Uint32 wakeEvent = (Uint32)-1;
+	if (wakeEvent == (Uint32)-1)
+		wakeEvent = SDL_RegisterEvents(1);
+	if (wakeEvent != (Uint32)-1)
+	{
+		SDL_Event ev {};
+		ev.type = wakeEvent;
+		SDL_PushEvent(&ev);
+	}
 }
 
 void Window::processPostedFunctions()
